<jmeterTestPlan version="1.2" properties="5.0" jmeter="5.6.2">
  <hashTree>
    <TestPlan guiclass="TestPlanGui" testclass="TestPlan" testname="TST-029 Delivery Guarantee, Retry, DLQ" enabled="true">
      <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">Task 24 (Wave 17 QE Harness). See README.md for the invariants (I1-I6) this plan asserts, and for why I2's broker restart is real (docker compose restart broker) rather than a Toxiproxy severance, and run-gated to full runs only rather than left unimplemented. The "Restart Broker And Recheck DLQ" JSR223Sampler in the TearDown group is the ONLY step that ever touches the broker container, and it is guarded by HarnessConfig.smokeMode() (the same single source of truth tst-031/tst-034/tst-035's own plan.jmx and this module's own assert-dlq.groovy already use, not a raw System.getenv comparison of its own) -- Tst029ModuleTest always runs with HARNESS_SMOKE_MODE=true, so that guard is exactly what keeps this module's own automated test from ever restarting a developer's running stack.</stringProp>
